      "content": "I understand your concerns, but in this case, it's better to take precautions. Sitting for long periods can certainly cause discomfort, but the sharp pain in your calf could be a sign of a more serious issue. Still, I'm not saying a hospital visit is necessary, but I would recommend ice and elevation to help reduce pain and swelling. You can try icing the area with a cold compress, elevating your leg, and taking regular breaks to stretch and move around. If the pain persists or worsens, consider having a friend or family member observe you until morning, just in case.",
